<main>
  <.link href={~p"/"}>Back to To</.link>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: October 29, 2026</p>
  <p>
    To, hosted at town.fly.dev, is a private shared task app for two configured
    household accounts. This policy explains how the app handles information.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect and use</h2>
  <p>
    We use your Google account identifier, verified email address, and basic
    profile information to sign you in and restrict access. We store your account
    details and Google authorization credentials so the app can connect to Google
    Tasks without asking you to sign in each time. We do not receive your Google
    password.
  </p>
  <p>
    We store lists, task titles and descriptions, assignments, dates, completion
    status, and records of who created or last changed a task. If you enable
    notifications, we also store your browser's notification subscription details,
    timezone, and reminder preferences to deliver task notifications.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app and its hosting provider may process technical request information,
    including IP addresses, browser information, and operational logs, to run,
    troubleshoot, and protect the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Tasks and household sharing</h2>
  <p>
    With your permission, To reads tasks from Google Tasks when you import them
    and creates, updates, or deletes Google Tasks as part of task synchronization.
    This can include task titles, notes, due dates, completion status, and task
    identifiers. Both authorized household users can see and edit shared lists
    and tasks, including tasks you import from Google.
  </p>
  <p>
    To's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">
      Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.
    We use Google data to provide the app's task features, not for advertising or
    training general-purpose artificial intelligence models.
  </p>

  <h2>Service providers and disclosures</h2>
  <p>
    Fly.io hosts the app and its database. Google processes sign-in and Google
    Tasks requests. When notifications are enabled, your browser's push provider
    processes notification delivery. Task titles may appear in notifications on
    your device, including its lock screen, depending on your device settings.
    These providers also handle information under their own privacy policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information or use it for advertising. Information
    may also be disclosed when required by law or when necessary to investigate
    abuse or protect the service, consistent with applicable Google data-use rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and security</h2>
  <p>
    To uses a sign-in cookie that can last up to 400 days and is renewed when you
    return, along with browser storage needed for app features. The app does not
    include advertising trackers or third-party analytics. We use HTTPS, signed
    sign-in cookies, and encryption for stored Google refresh credentials. No
    system can guarantee complete security.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Account and task information is retained to operate the shared app. Deleting
    a task or list removes it from active views but does not automatically erase
    its database record. Backups may retain earlier copies. Signing out or
    revoking Google access does not delete information already stored in To.
    Copies in Google Tasks are also subject to Google's policies and your Google
    account controls.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can sign out, clear your browser's cookies, disable notifications in
    Settings or your browser, and revoke To's access through your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google account connections</a>.
    To ask questions or request access, correction, or permanent deletion of
    stored information, email <a href="mailto:63poz3umf@mozmail.com">63poz3umf@mozmail.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when these practices change. If Google data would be
    used for a new purpose, we will provide notice and obtain consent as required
    by Google's policies and applicable law before doing so.
  </p>
</main>
